  "caption": "3am, and Quinn's hand had fallen asleep again. Shake it like a maraca, the tingles fade, then they're back the next night.\n\nNight-time numbness in the thumb, index and middle fingers that eases with a shake is a classic carpal tunnel pattern. Keeping the wrist bent for long periods, like curled up in bed, can raise pressure on the median nerve. Typing often isn't the main cause.\n\nWhat often helps: a neutral wrist splint overnight for at least six weeks, gentle nerve glides, less vibrating-tool use and forceful gripping, and avoiding long bent-wrist positions. Your GP can check for other contributors.\n\nGet it checked if numbness is constant, the thumb muscle looks smaller, the little finger is numb, or symptoms spread up the arm.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
